@@ -6,6 +6,24 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- **Breaking:** `grep` content pages now count match regions instead of rendered match/context lines. Do not reuse 0.7.0 offsets with new `next_offset` values; count and file-list modes still paginate by file.
+- Added `[tool_output].grep_output_byte_cap` (32,768 bytes) and `overview_output_byte_cap` (8,192 bytes), including status and continuation text. Config schema 6 adds these keys without replacing existing values.
+- `grep_max_columns` now budgets match-centered excerpts with original byte positions instead of discarding long matching lines. `0` removes only the per-line limit.
+
+### Improved
+
+- Keep grep matches with requested context, deduplicate overlapping context, and retain positioned evidence when a single match exceeds the output budget.
+- Support literal grep with `fixed_strings` / `-F`, report partial searches after read/walk failures, and distinguish whole-search from page counts.
+- Allow explicit-path `read`, `find`, and `grep` without initial guidance; include the running package version once in `initial_instructions`.
+- Apply workspace scope before all search candidate collection with a score-free path filter; preserve the public query context and existing index schema without reindexing.
+- Bound all overview formats and per-folder/file symbol lists; omit `read_suggestion` only for proven complete, unambiguous source output.
+
+### Internal
+
+- Add regression coverage and an isolated Codex comparison runner against the 0.7.0 tag; preserve the existing OpenCode harness.
+
